      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}}{[{e}^{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{x})}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2}{x{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
